{"kind":"assert","text":"U4-B plan check, on your dc13b60b. The driver is ready in my scratchpad (persistent profile, before and after phases; the invitation enters only the page field, and the evidence is scrubbed). I start the before reads after your END. Two points before then:\n\n1. The Lending join after the upgrade needs a second invitation. Browser storage is per origin. The one invitation enrolls this browser on counter-upgrade.inguz.space, and lending-shelf.inguz.space has its own IndexedDB, so the Lending page there has no device key. LS-7 also showed that the Lending 0.4.0 page cannot join (its client predates GW-1), so I do not join Lending before the upgrade. The before read records what the page shows without a join. For \"the screen join and the stepladder projection after\", I need either a second invitation for @upgrade-witness used on lending-shelf.inguz.space after the upgrade to 0.6.0, or your ruling that the Lending after read is the pre-join page plus the stepladder read through the CLI. Which one?\n\n2. The MCP cards in U4-B. A card read needs an MCP host with a member session, and the member's key lives only in this browser. I plan to cover the screens in the browser and leave the cards out of U4-B, unless you name a home and a host for them.\n\nBefore phase: the Counter page enrolls with invitation 1, joins the count, and I record the footer (0.6.0 has no data-release line, so I expect none), the custody records, the count and a screenshot. The Lending 0.4.0 page is read with no join.","body":{"to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"}}